{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Why have You dealt ill, etc., and why, etc.</b> It is difficult: why does he begin with the complaint over the harm done, and only afterward with the complaint over the withholding of benefit — for he should have said ״לָמָּה לֹא מָצָאתִי חֵן״ etc. first, and then ״לָמָּה הֲרֵעֹתָ״ etc.? However, the intent is according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Sifrei 91) on the verse ״לֵךְ נְחֵה אֶת הָעָם״, that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses: ״My children are stubborn, they are burdensome, etc.; they curse you, they stone you with stones״ etc. — thus far their language. And regarding this, Moses' statement comes here: <b>Why have You dealt ill</b> — meaning, You have cast upon me this evil to suffer the troubles caused by Your children; and after I accepted it, it would have been fitting to find favor in Your eyes to give me a helper to bear with me under the great yoke — yet this You did not do, for You placed the entire burden upon me. And he said <b>לֹא מָצָתִי</b> — lacking a ׳alef׳, to say: even מִצּוּי (a mere trace), meaning, even a small amount of favor I did not attain." "<b>Or</b> it may intend as follows: <b>Why have You dealt ill</b> as I explained, and His saying <b>and why have I not found</b> — meaning, since You have placed upon me the yoke of this matter, I have grounds to demand: why have I not found favor, inasmuch as You placed upon me the burden of all the people. And the meaning of the lamed of <b>לָשׂוּם</b> is the lamed of causation. And Moses said this because he saw that he sought — according to the words of the midrash that we wrote nearby — that He not give them meat and not kill them, yet he did not find favor in the eyes of HaShem to have his prayer accepted. He also saw what befell him because of them: that they caused him death in the wilderness, and how many branches of sorrow encompassed him from them — when it should not have been so, for it would have been fitting to compensate him for his toil and his burdens."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "The missing alef in לֹא מָצָתִי (instead of לֹא מָצָאתִי) creates a wordplay with מִצּוּי (a small amount/trace), which depends on the defective spelling; rendered literally to preserve the argument."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:07:39.732696044Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}